  "source": "The Montgomery ladder (and the related 'double-and-add-always' idea) is a standard constant-pattern scalar multiplication technique; see for example 'Guide to Elliptic Curve Cryptography' (Hankerson, Menezes, Vanstone) and common Curve25519 discussions. Vectors below are project-internal and cross-checked against the `ecdsa` Python library for secp256k1 and an independent script for the toy curve.",
